  <h1>About</h1>
  <p>
    Korea, Explained is a blog written for English-speaking readers who are curious
    about Korea — its culture, food, travel, and everyday life. Posts start as
    AI-assisted drafts and are reviewed and edited by a human before publishing,
    with the goal of adding original, practical detail rather than just summarizing
    what's already online.
  </p>
  <p>
    This site is written and edited by Chris Kim, who reviews, fact-checks, and
    edits every post before it's published.
  </p>
